diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index d72c8c7..d49070a 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -98,7 +98,28 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (authorized via the queue `call` ability, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); Both call paths enforce the queue `call` ability (see [Queue Management and Access](#queue-management-and-access)); HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+
+### Queue Management and Access
+
+Domain actions only (no UI yet). All authorization lives in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy`.
+
+**Lifecycle** (owner/admin of the entity only; employees, members of other entities and non-members get `AuthorizationException` and nothing is written):
+
+- `App\Actions\CreateQueue` — name is trimmed, 1–255 chars; slug defaults to `Str::slug(name)` and an explicit slug is slugified too; new queues are active.
+- `App\Actions\UpdateQueue` — any combination of name, slug and active flag (`null` = unchanged).
+- Slugs are unique **within an entity** (the same slug may exist in another entity). A duplicate — including one caught by the DB unique index in a race — is a `ValidationException`.
+- **No hard delete.** A queue is retired by deactivation (`is_active = false`): its tickets are preserved and issuing or calling on it keeps failing with `InactiveQueueException`. There is no delete/remove/destroy queue action.
+
+**Per-queue access.** Employees may call tickets only on queues where a manager granted them access (`queue_access` row). The only permission today is `call` (`App\Enums\QueuePermission`). `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` (owner/admin only — an employee cannot grant themselves) sets the permissions of a membership on a queue: a non-empty list upserts the grant, an empty list revokes it. Unknown permissions or non-string entries, or a membership and queue of different entities, are a `ValidationException` and nothing is stored. Grants and revokes are written to the `audit` log channel (`queue.access.granted`, `queue.access.revoked`, with `actor_id`, `queue_id`, `entity_membership_id`); revoking a non-existent grant logs nothing.
+
+| Ability | Who |
+| ------- | --- |
+| `create` (entity) | Owner/admin of that entity |
+| `update`, `manageAccess` | Owner/admin of the queue's entity |
+| `call` | Owner/admin of the queue's entity (no grant needed); employee only with a `queue_access` row for **that** queue whose `permissions` is an array containing `call` (a corrupted non-array value denies); everyone else denied |
+
+**Call enforcement.** `CallNextTicket` authorizes `call` after locking the queue and checking it is active (all call modes). `Ticket::call()` locks, rejects inactive queues (`InactiveQueueException`), then authorizes (`AuthorizationException`, even if the ticket was already called), then applies the "only waiting tickets" `LogicException`.
 
 ### Priority
 
